# AegisFlow settings. Copy to .env (mode 0600) or, better, run `bash harness/configure_keys.sh`
# (hidden prompts) or use the Aegis Console's Settings drawer. Values in the process environment
# take precedence over .env. Every service stays disabled while its key is empty, and nothing calls
# it; tests always use local listeners and read only their own .env, never the environment.
#
# Not a credential: AEGIS_ANE_KEEPWARM_MS (environment only, default 1000, 0 disables) is how long
# aegis-daemon lets a CoreML model sit idle before it runs one all-zero keep-warm prediction.

# Nemotron provider for build-recovery tiers 1-2 (Nemotron Super / Ultra). NEBIUS_BASE_URL picks one
# of the allowlisted OpenAI-compatible providers; empty means Nebius Token Factory. Any other value
# disables the remote tiers (http(s)://127.0.0.1, localhost or [::1] is accepted for local tests):
#   https://api.tokenfactory.nebius.com/v1   Nebius Token Factory (default). Keys: https://tokenfactory.nebius.com/
#   https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1      NVIDIA NIM. Keys (nvapi-...): https://build.nvidia.com
#   https://openrouter.ai/api/v1             OpenRouter. Keys: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# The console's Settings drawer offers the same three as a selector; `bash harness/configure_keys.sh`
# offers them as a menu.
NEBIUS_BASE_URL=
# API key for the selected provider (the name stays NEBIUS_API_KEY for compatibility). It is sent
# only to NEBIUS_BASE_URL. Switching provider from the console needs the new provider's key in the
# same save.
NEBIUS_API_KEY=
# Tier model ids. Empty means the provider's default where one is confirmed:
#   Nebius Token Factory: nvidia/Llama-3_3-Nemotron-Super-49B-v1 / nvidia/Llama-3_1-Nemotron-Ultra-253B-v1
#   NVIDIA NIM: tier 1 required (no Llama-Nemotron Super 49B in its /models list), tier 2
#               nvidia/llama-3.1-nemotron-ultra-253b-v1
#   OpenRouter: both required (pick Nemotron ids from https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models)
# A required id left empty keeps the remote tiers disabled. The console's "Test Nemotron provider"
# lists the Nemotron ids the selected provider serves.
NEBIUS_TIER1_MODEL=
NEBIUS_TIER2_MODEL=

# Tavily search: documentation retrieval for recovery tier 2. Key at https://app.tavily.com/
TAVILY_API_KEY=

# PayPal Sandbox REST app (Orders v2). Create an app at
# https://developer.paypal.com/dashboard/applications/sandbox
# The console submits at most 25 Sandbox orders per daemon run, and only Cedar-allowed ones.
# Left empty (or both set to local-sandbox), allowed orders go to the daemon's own local
# Orders v2 gateway at http://127.0.0.1:4173/paypal-sandbox instead: an emulation, nothing is
# sent to PayPal.
PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Team-approval cards. Incoming-webhook URLs are secrets (anyone with the URL can post).
# Mattermost: Integrations > Incoming Webhooks. Slack: https://api.slack.com/messaging/webhooks
AEGIS_MATTERMOST_WEBHOOK_URL=
AEGIS_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Mattermost interactive-action callback that receives Approve/Reject clicks (optional)
AEGIS_APPROVAL_CALLBACK_URL=
